Strong positive cases are this-> member access, patent language and a few
fixed English phrases. Strong negative cases are short Arabic thaa/dhal
pieces and their continuations, with much weaker responses in Persian.
Greek theta and a few other th-spellings supply smaller rules. Everything
else is zero; document boundaries clear the short continuation memory.
