        (Is, Are, Was, Do, Can, Would); 0 with a leading space (" is", " will")
  +1.5  subordinating opener (If, When, While, As)
  +2.7  money and trade words (price, cash, supply, sale, deposit, tax, income, pay)
  +2.2  common punctuation (',', '.', '#', '-', ')', '%', '$', '+', '=')
  +1.8  the digit 0 (other digits about zero)
  +0.3  other symbols
  +2.0  a run of spaces (tab-containing whitespace -0.5)
  -2.3  an opening bracket that starts a code type ("(String", "[Object", "<int")
  -2.0  a C preprocessor line opener ("#include")
  -2.9  weekday names (Monday ... Sunday)
  -2.2  code type or class words (Object, String, Integer, public, def, null) and
        people and role nouns (human, child, student, customer, author)
  -1.5  first names (John, William, David, Kevin) and greetings or imperative openers
        (Hello, Welcome, Let, Wait, Show, Find)
  -1.0  subject pronouns and prepositions (You, We, They, That, Your, To, With, From, In)
  -0.4  the, a, it
  -0.4  a token containing a newline
  0     everything else, including most ordinary words, and every position inside a document
Each word in a group scatters by about +/-1 around the group's value, so this program
explains only a part of the variance (about 0.2 of it on evaluation rows); most of it is
specific to individual tokens and is not captured here.
"""
